  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1107 PM CST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nExpect mostly clear skies through tomorrow with surface high pressure \nbeing the dominate feature across the Plains. Winds will be light \nand from the north through this morning becoming light and variable \nthis afternoon into this evening. Winds then shift to the southeast \ntomorrow with a slight increase in speed. As for temperatures, lows \nthis morning will dip to around 40 degrees with highs this afternoon \nin the mid to upper 60s. Lows tonight will once again dip to around \n40 degrees with highs Monday around 70 degrees. \n\nThe remainder of the forecast looks dry as an upper level ridge \nmoves over the Plains early next week with high pressure being the \ndominate feature at the surface. Mid range models show a cold front \nmove through the area mid week. At this time the NBM depicts no \nincrease in precipitation as this boundary moves through. We then go \nback into a ridge pattern keeping western Kansas dry. Highs through \nthis period will generally be in the low 60s to low 70s with lows in \nthe upper 30s to 40s.",
